==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ljúka}}, {{m|non|lúka}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*lūkaną|*leukaną, *lūkaną|t=to shut, lock}}. Of the two forms, ''ljúka'' and ''lúka'', the latter is attested earlier.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈljuːka/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|uːka|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|lauk|luku|lokið}} {{+obj|is|dat}}

# to [[finish]], to [[end]], to [[conclude]] {{gl|to bring to an end}} {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{syn|is|enda|binda enda á}}
# to [[complete]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{syn|is|klára}}
# to [[finalise]]/[[finalize]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{syn|is|ganga frá}}
# to [[expire]] {{q|of a limited period of time}}
#: {{syn|is|renna út}}
# to [[close]] (e.g. one's eyes) {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{syn|is|loka|lykja}} 

